### S1 surfaces — Prepare, Create, GetOrder, GetOperation, projection rebuild
### Routes and bodies are generated from the running host (openapi.json in this folder).
### Tokens are issued by IdentityServer; never paste a real token into evidence.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@backofficeToken = {{$processEnv ORDERING_BACKOFFICE_TOKEN}}
@otaPanelToken = {{$processEnv ORDERING_OTAPANEL_TOKEN}}
@otaToken = {{$processEnv ORDERING_OTA_TOKEN}}
@offerId = REPLACE-WITH-A-PRICED-OFFER-ID
@financialCustomerId = 100
@sellingOfficeId = 10

### 1. backoffice — prepare (authenticated, authz_surface=backoffice, office must match the token)
POST {{host}}/backoffice/v1/order-preparations
Authorization: Bearer {{backofficeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: prepare-backoffice-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "offerId": "{{offerId}}",
  "financialCustomerId": "{{financialCustomerId}}",
  "sellingOfficeId": "{{sellingOfficeId}}",
  "clientReference": null
}

### 2. backoffice — create from the accepted preparation (no owner call)
POST {{host}}/backoffice/v1/orders/from-offer
Authorization: Bearer {{backofficeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: create-backoffice-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "preparationId": "REPLACE-WITH-preparationId",
  "acceptedSnapshotDigest": "REPLACE-WITH-acceptedSnapshotDigest",
  "acceptedAt": "2026-09-18T09:00:00Z",
  "financialCustomerId": "{{financialCustomerId}}",
  "sellingOfficeId": "{{sellingOfficeId}}",
  "travelerBindings": [
    {
      "sourceTravellerRef": "ADT-1",
      "clientTravelerRef": "CLIENT-ADT-1",
      "givenName": "Sample",
      "surname": "Traveler",
      "passengerTypeCode": "ADT",
      "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
      "guardianClientTravelerRef": null
    }
  ],
  "contacts": [
    { "role": "Primary", "email": "traveler@example.invalid", "phone": null }
  ],
  "clientReference": null
}

### 3. backoffice — read the local order (protected traveler/contact payloads included)
GET {{host}}/backoffice/v1/orders/REPLACE-WITH-orderId?minRevision=1
Authorization: Bearer {{backofficeToken}}

### 4. backoffice — read the durable operation
GET {{host}}/backoffice/v1/operations/REPLACE-WITH-operationId
Authorization: Bearer {{backofficeToken}}

### 5. otapanel — prepare (customer and office come from the token only)
POST {{host}}/otapanel/v1/order-preparations
Authorization: Bearer {{otaPanelToken}}
Idempotency-Key: prepare-otapanel-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "offerId": "{{offerId}}",
  "clientReference": null
}

### 6. ota (platform surface "api") — prepare for the token customer
POST {{host}}/ota/v1/order-preparations
Authorization: Bearer {{otaToken}}
Idempotency-Key: prepare-ota-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "offerId": "{{offerId}}",
  "clientReference": null
}

### 7. service — prepare (no token in the current platform phase; explicit customer scope)
POST {{host}}/service/v1/order-preparations
Idempotency-Key: prepare-service-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "offerId": "{{offerId}}",
  "financialCustomerId": "{{financialCustomerId}}",
  "sellingOfficeId": null,
  "clientReference": null
}

### 8. service — read the local order (protected personal fields are always redacted here)
GET {{host}}/service/v1/orders/REPLACE-WITH-orderId

### 9. internal — rebuild the order projection (operational route, no token in this phase)
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/orders/REPLACE-WITH-orderId/projection-rebuilds
Idempotency-Key: rebuild-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{}
